-- title:
--   Correspondences with equal fibre supports have isomorphic composita
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and let $F_0$, $F$, $F'$ be fields equipped with $K$-algebra structures, each satisfying `IsCurveOver K`: every nonzero element has an associated degree-zero divisor recording its orders at all places, every place has residue field finite over $K$, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one; in addition $F$ and $F'$ are essentially of finite type over $K$. Here a place of a field $E$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $E$, distinct from $E$, containing the image of $K$ and a principal ideal ring, and a divisor is a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on places. Let $\varphi_0,\varphi_1 : F_0 \to F$ and $\varphi'_0,\varphi'_1 : F_0 \to F'$ be $K$-algebra maps, each integral as a ring homomorphism and each finite in the sense that the target is a finite module over $F_0$ along the map. Assume that for every place $P$ of $F_0$ the divisor obtained from the indicator divisor $P \mapsto 1$ by pulling back along $\varphi_0$ and pushing forward along $\varphi_1$ has the same support as the divisor obtained from it by pulling back along $\varphi'_0$ and pushing forward along $\varphi'_1$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $\theta$ from the subfield of $F$ generated by the union of the ranges of $\varphi_0$ and $\varphi_1$ onto the subfield of $F'$ generated by the union of the ranges of $\varphi'_0$ and $\varphi'_1$ with $\theta(\varphi_0 x) = \varphi'_0 x$ and $\theta(\varphi_1 x) = \varphi'_1 x$ for all $x \in F_0$.
--
--   In classical language: a correspondence on the curve with function field $F_0$ given by two finite maps from a curve $X$ is determined up to isomorphism of its image in $C \times C$ by the set-theoretic fibres $\mathrm{supp}\,(\varphi_1)_*(\varphi_0)^*[P]$, the compositum of the two images being recovered as the function field of that image. It serves as the common core of the uniqueness statements for Hecke towers, [`CerednikDrinfeld.HeckeTower.correspondence_eq_of_support_eq_of_finrankAlong_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.HeckeTower.correspondence_eq_of_support_eq_of_finrankAlong_eq) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.HeckeTower.exists_algEquiv_forall_comp_phi_eq_of_correspondence_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.HeckeTower.exists_algEquiv_forall_comp_phi_eq_of_correspondence_eq), which supplement it with a multiplicity count.
-- source:
